# HQL — Hyper Query Language

HQL is a statically typed expression and query language. A program is
type-checked before it is evaluated. Querying is one capability: the intended
language also constructs values, evaluates functions, transforms data,
validates constraints, and returns typed results. Its direction is closer to
Rust, Kusto, Scala, Haskell, or even Lean, than to SQL; its operations take
their inspiration from jq and SQL, among others. The language cards live under
[doc/wiki/hql/](hql/).

HQL operates on a typed model of docs, cards, metadata, document structure,
namespaces, relations, and knowledge graphs. Sources reach the language through
extensions, and HyperMarkDown is one of them: an `.hmd` file and an `.md` file
are both documents, and a card is the document that represents a piece of
knowledge rather than the one written in a particular format. See
[[hmd-integration]] and [[design-direction]]. But we also work with YAML/JSON documents as `Collection<Data>`.

The working bootstrap evaluates Int, Float and Bool literals and same-type
addition. It has no knowledge-source integration yet. See the
[system declarations](../models/requirements/bootstrap.md) and
[[hql/design-status]] for what is designed but not built.
